  "prompt": "=== Chain-of-thought analysis prompt ===\nYou are a software requirements analyst preparing a UML state machine model.\n\nAnalyze the requirement and extract only the modeling facts needed for a state transition diagram. Keep the analysis concise and evidence-based.\n\nReturn the analysis using exactly these headings:\nStates:\nInitial state:\nFinal states:\nEvents or conditions:\nTransitions:\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n\nDo not write PlantUML in this step.\n\nRequirement:\nDigital Watch — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall allow the user to view and adjust the time.\n2. The system shall enable the user to switch between changing hour, minutes, alarm hour, and alarm minutes by pressing a button.\n3. The system shall allow the user to increase values while adjusting time settings.\n4. The system shall provide an alarm feature that can be turned on or off by the user.\n5. The system shall support when the set alarm time matches the current time, the system shall trigger the alarm to ring.\n6. The system shall allow the user to stop the alarm by pressing a specific button.\n7. The system shall have a light feature that turns on when the user presses a button and turns off when the button is released.\n\n=== Chain-of-thought analysis response ===\nStates:\n- Time Adjustment Mode\n- Alarm Setting Mode\n- Light On Mode\n\nInitial state:\nTime Adjustment Mode\n\nFinal states:\nNone explicitly defined, but could be implied as exiting all modes.\n\nEvents or conditions:\n- Press Button 1 (for time adjustment)\n- Press Button 2 (for alarm setting)\n- Press Button 3 (to increase values)\n- Turn Alarm On/Off\n- Set Alarm Time\n- Current Time Matches Alarm Time\n- Press Stop Alarm Button\n- Press Light Control Button\n\nTransitions:\n- From Time Adjustment Mode to Alarm Setting Mode: Press Button 1, then press Button 2\n- From Time Adjustment Mode to Light On Mode: Press Light Control Button and hold\n- From Alarm Setting Mode to Time Adjustment Mode: Press Button 1, then release Button 2\n- From Light On Mode to Time Adjustment Mode: Release Light Control Button\n\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n- The exact behavior when the alarm time matches the current time (triggering the alarm) is not clearly defined in terms of state transitions.\n- How pressing specific buttons affects the values being adjusted (hours, minutes, etc.) is not detailed.\n- The sequence and conditions for exiting modes are not specified.\n\n=== PlantUML generation prompt ===\nYou are a UML modeling expert.\n\nConvert the requirement and the structured analysis into one UML state transition diagram in PlantUML format.\n\nOutput Rules:\n- Generate ONLY valid PlantUML code.\n- Start with @startuml and end with @enduml.\n- Use [*] for exactly one initial transition.\n- Include at least one final transition to [*].\n- Use clear transition labels when requirement evidence exists.\n- Do not include explanations, analysis, or markdown fences.\n\nRequirement:\nDigital Watch — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall allow the user to view and adjust the time.\n2. The system shall enable the user to switch between changing hour, minutes, alarm hour, and alarm minutes by pressing a button.\n3. The system shall allow the user to increase values while adjusting time settings.\n4. The system shall provide an alarm feature that can be turned on or off by the user.\n5. The system shall support when the set alarm time matches the current time, the system shall trigger the alarm to ring.\n6. The system shall allow the user to stop the alarm by pressing a specific button.\n7. The system shall have a light feature that turns on when the user presses a button and turns off when the button is released.\n\nStructured analysis from step 1:\nStates:\n- Time Adjustment Mode\n- Alarm Setting Mode\n- Light On Mode\n\nInitial state:\nTime Adjustment Mode\n\nFinal states:\nNone explicitly defined, but could be implied as exiting all modes.\n\nEvents or conditions:\n- Press Button 1 (for time adjustment)\n- Press Button 2 (for alarm setting)\n- Press Button 3 (to increase values)\n- Turn Alarm On/Off\n- Set Alarm Time\n- Current Time Matches Alarm Time\n- Press Stop Alarm Button\n- Press Light Control Button\n\nTransitions:\n- From Time Adjustment Mode to Alarm Setting Mode: Press Button 1, then press Button 2\n- From Time Adjustment Mode to Light On Mode: Press Light Control Button and hold\n- From Alarm Setting Mode to Time Adjustment Mode: Press Button 1, then release Button 2\n- From Light On Mode to Time Adjustment Mode: Release Light Control Button\n\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n- The exact behavior when the alarm time matches the current time (triggering the alarm) is not clearly defined in terms of state transitions.\n- How pressing specific buttons affects the values being adjusted (hours, minutes, etc.) is not detailed.\n- The sequence and conditions for exiting modes are not specified.\n\nNow return only the final PlantUML.\n",
